content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I pay for my groceries?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at the supermarket. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "checkout "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the place in a supermarket where you pay for your groceries  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's go to the checkout line."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cashier "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who works in a store and collects money "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I give the cashier my money."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "customer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who buys things  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This lane is for customers with 10 items or less."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coupon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small piece of paper that lets you pay less "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a coupon for $1.00."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to swipe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pull a card through a machine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Swipe your card here please."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cash "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "money "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am paying in cash."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "debit card "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a plastic card you can use to pay for things "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are you going to pay with your debit card?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "credit card "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a plastic card you use to buy things and pay for later "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I pay with my credit card?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob10aud09"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Demonstrative Adjectives and Pronouns "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Demonstratives are words that show the person or thing you are talking about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " The demonstratives are: <span class=\"strong\"> this, that, these</span> and <span class=\"strong\"> those</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Demonstratives tell us about number (singular or plural) and distance (near or far). <br/><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> Those </span>sweet potatoes look great.  Pass me one please. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are <span class=\"italic\"> demonstrative adjectives</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> demonstrative pronouns</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A demonstrative adjective tells us about the noun. It comes before the noun.<br /><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> This</span> potato is good. <span class=\"strong\">That</span> potato is not good. <br/> How much do <span class=\"strong\">these</span> potatoes weigh?  I like <span class=\"strong\"> those</span> sweet potatoes. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A demonstrative pronoun replaces a noun. It is on its own. <br /> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> This</span>  is good.  <span class=\"strong\">That</span> is bad. <br/>I like <span class=\"strong\"> these</span>. I don't like <span class=\"strong\">those</span>. </span>"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le04ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (6-8 lines) between a cashier and a customer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use 4 target words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Imperative."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use a demonstrative adjective and a demonstrative pronoun."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading the dialogue aloud with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I use the correct expressions in a supermarket."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use words related to the checkout line."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I point things out in the checkout line."}]}], "type": "sena"}